doc:Factsid1_53 None:has_text_value "Because the hydraulic oil initially supplied by the factory is basically mineral oil, when it mixes with biodegradable oil, the hydraulic oil becomes cloudy, precipitation occurs, filters clog, valves malfunction, and other defects may occur. To prevent the mixing of biodegradable oil and mineral oil, the manual specifies multiple oil changes as part of the oil change procedure. Given this background, the oxidation of lubricating oil due to the low oxidation stability of biodegradable oils can contribute to preventive maintenance if oil condition monitoring is applied. Therefore, we examined the temperature characteristics of biodegradable oils and the correlation with oil analysis of oxidized oil using an oil sensor. We also investigated the sliding characteristics when the oil was oxidized and examined whether biodegradable oil and mineral oil can be distinguished based on the characteristics obtained from the study." .
_:d0874525dfdb46b907a92c13e5a176c rdf:reifies <<( doc:Factsid1_53 None:has_text_value "Because the hydraulic oil initially supplied by the factory is basically mineral oil, when it mixes with biodegradable oil, the hydraulic oil becomes cloudy, precipitation occurs, filters clog, valves malfunction, and other defects may occur. To prevent the mixing of biodegradable oil and mineral oil, the manual specifies multiple oil changes as part of the oil change procedure. Given this background, the oxidation of lubricating oil due to the low oxidation stability of biodegradable oils can contribute to preventive maintenance if oil condition monitoring is applied. Therefore, we examined the temperature characteristics of biodegradable oils and the correlation with oil analysis of oxidized oil using an oil sensor. We also investigated the sliding characteristics when the oil was oxidized and examined whether biodegradable oil and mineral oil can be distinguished based on the characteristics obtained from the study." )>> ;
	prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:20c2316d1660 .
